			"Message": "build(deps-dev): bump @types/serviceworker from 0.0.176 to 0.0.178\n\nBumps [@types/serviceworker](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript-DOM-Lib-Generator) from 0.0.176 to 0.0.178.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript-DOM-Lib-Generator/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript-DOM-Lib-Generator/compare/@types/serviceworker@0.0.176...@types/serviceworker@0.0.178)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/serviceworker\"\n  dependency-version: 0.0.178\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "3a20f4c6ff18eb8d6816f4a64fa5923c653add5a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-20T13:18:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				44,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(policy): adjust script URL validation regex to support nested paths and MJS modules\n\nThe script URL validation regex in the Worker Trusted Types policy has been updated to be more permissive and accurate. The previous pattern `/^\\/[^\\/\\\\:]+\\\\.js(\\\\?.*)?$/` only allowed single-level paths (no additional slashes) and only supported .js extensions.\n\nKey changes made:\n1. **Removed the slash restriction**: The character class `[^\\/\\\\:]` has been changed to `[^\\\\:]`, allowing forward slashes (`/`) within the path. This enables support for nested directory structures in script URLs (e.g., `/scripts/app/main.js`).\n2. **Added MJS support**: The extension pattern now accepts both `.js` and `.mjs` files via the alternation `(js|mjs)`, accommodating JavaScript modules alongside traditional scripts.\n\nThe regex `/^\\/[^\\\\:]+\\\\.(js|mjs)(\\\\?.*)?$/` now correctly validates:\n- Nested paths like `/admin/panel/app.js`\n- Module scripts like `/lib/utils.mjs`\n- Both extensions with optional query strings\n\nAdditionally, a minor refactoring was applied to the ESBuild configuration plugin's conditional logic for the clean operation, replacing a `switch` statement with a more direct conditional expression for clarity.\n\nThese changes ensure the Worker's security policy aligns with real-world URL structures while maintaining protection against unsafe script injection patterns.",
			"SHA": "02306ed8a3cf4664c6d2a858612ac365d3252548"
		}
	],
